WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.840
At the end of the Warring States period, Qin grew stronger and stronger, and the other six states were afraid.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:13.440
Crown Prince Dan of Yan was deeply worried that Qin would attack Yan.

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:18.240
Prince Dan found a brave assassin named Jing Ke.

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:24.320
He hid a dagger inside a map and asked Jing Ke to assassinate Ying Zheng, the King of Qin.

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:30.920
Carrying the long map, Jing Ke set out bravely for Qin.

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:36.120
In the magnificent Qin palace, Jing Ke presented the map to the King.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:39.840
As the map unrolled, the dagger was revealed!

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.640
Jing Ke chased after the King of Qin!

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:47.040
The King dodged around a great pillar — a heart-stopping scene.

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:52.800
Sadly, the assassination failed in the end. Jing Ke did not succeed.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:59.070
Later, Ying Zheng unified the six states and became the great Qin Shi Huang.
